public with sharing class LineItemDiscountHandler {

    /**
     * For every new line without an explicit Discount, apply the standard
     * discount for its product by delegating to PricingRules (owned by the
     * pricing team; we never duplicate its logic here).
     *
     * PricingRules.standardDiscountFor() issues one SOQL query per call
     * (it queries Product2 by Id). To stay bulk-safe when a single insert
     * batch contains many lines for the same product (as CPQ quotes
     * typically do), we only call PricingRules once per distinct
     * Product2Id and cache the result for the rest of the batch. This
     * does not change or duplicate any pricing logic - it simply avoids
     * asking PricingRules the same question more than once per product
     * within a single trigger execution.
     *
     * Note: if a batch somehow contains more than ~100 *distinct*
     * products all needing a default discount, this would still exceed
     * the synchronous SOQL limit. In that edge case the fix would need to
     * come from the pricing team exposing a bulk method such as
     *   Map<Id, Decimal> standardDiscountsFor(Set<Id> productIds)
     * For the realistic CPQ case of up to 200 lines (typically repeating
     * a smaller set of products), per-product caching is sufficient.
     */
    public static void applyStandardDiscounts(List<OpportunityLineItem> newLines) {
        Map<Id, Decimal> discountByProduct = new Map<Id, Decimal>();

        for (OpportunityLineItem line : newLines) {
            if (line.Discount == null && line.Product2Id != null) {
                if (!discountByProduct.containsKey(line.Product2Id)) {
